{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q3333513","formula":"CH₅⁺","hill":"CH5","elements":["H","C"],"composition":{"C":1.0,"H":5.0},"names":{"en":"Methanium"},"descriptions":{"en":"In chemistry, methanium is a complex positive ion with formula [CH5]+ (metastable transitional form, a carbon atom covalently bonded to five hydrogen atoms) or [CH3(H2)]+ (fluxional form, namely a molecule with one carbon atom covalently bonded to three hydrogen atoms and one dihydrogen molecule), bearing a +1 electric charge. It is a superacid and one of the onium ions, indeed the simplest carbonium ion. It is highly unstable and highly reactive even upon having a complete octet, thus granting its superacidic properties."},"fame":8,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":1,"smiles":"[CH5+]","inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3333513","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Methanium","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"similar":[{"id":"Q37129","formula":"CH₄","names":{"en":"Methane","ru":"Метан","uk":"Метан"},"elements":["H","C"],"fame":119,"kind":"molecule"},{"id":"Q37497367","formula":"NH₅","names":{"en":"Nitrogen pentahydride"},"elements":["H","N"],"fame":4,"kind":null},{"id":"Q1216189","formula":"CH₄","names":{"en":"(2H4)methane"},"elements":["H","C"],"fame":2,"kind":"molecule"},{"id":"Q52858","formula":"C₂H₆","names":{"en":"Ethane","ru":"Этан","uk":"Етан"},"elements":["H","C"],"fame":82,"kind":"molecule"},{"id":"Q190901","formula":"H₄N⁺","names":{"en":"Ammonium cation","ru":"Аммоний","uk":"Амоній"},"elements":["H","N"],"fame":62,"kind":"molecule"},{"id":"Q3333706","formula":"CH₃⁺","names":{"en":"Methenium"},"elements":["H","C"],"fame":11,"kind":"molecule"},{"id":"Q6823951","formula":"CH